{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqq0frbreww","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"USER DIRECTIVE (2026-06-22): bench / eval harnesses must invoke the REAL production code path, never a reimplementation. Concrete anti-pattern being eliminated: the bench SDK's EdgeJudge + _EDGE_JUDGE_RUBRIC in bench/zonoid_bench/judge.py is a Python port of production's self-learn edge-judge (the prompt built in lib/headless-drain.js buildJudgePrompt, run in-process via provider.runJudgeLoop). Two independently maintained implementations of the SAME keep/prune edge decision drift silently and invalidate any parity claim. RULE: when production cannot be invoked from a bench/isolated context, REFACTOR PRODUCTION to expose the interface (e.g. a synchronous, node-scoped, bounded in-process judge drain reusing runJudgeLoop) and have the bench DRIVE it — do not copy the logic. Same rule governs autowire params: production should not gate autowire on a brittle cosine floor; drop the 0.55 SEMANTIC_AUTOWIRE_THRESHOLD (daemon.js:1675) to 0 so the eager-judge arbitrates, and the bench then runs prod defaults with zero override. Applies to ALL benches including Terminal-Bench (use the SDK agent_in_container mode, which drives the real daemon). Why: parity is only real if there is exactly one implementation. How to apply: for any future bench/eval work, drive real daemon endpoints + production libs; if blocked, add a production entrypoint rather than porting.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T02:28:46.848Z"}
